  "presentation_summary": [
    "Seventy-seven-year-old man underwent surgery for benign prostatic hyperplasia under sevoflurane anesthesia without succinylcholine.",
    "Morning vital signs were stable: BP 120/70 mmHg, HR 78/min, RR 20/min, and temperature 36.7 C.",
    "Ten minutes after arrival in the postanesthetic care unit he developed shivering, severe anxiety, stupor, masseter and arm rigidity, hyperventilation, BP 220/168 mmHg, HR 134/min, RR 30/min, temperature 38.1 C, and SpO2 98%.",
    "Ten minutes later temperature rose to 39.8 C with worsening rigidity.",
    "ABG and biochemical tests showed pH 7.35, PaCO2 33 mmHg, PaO2 79 mmHg, bicarbonate 18.2 mmol/L, CK 1735 U/L, LDH 487 U/L, and myoglobin 2968 ng/mL.",
    "He received ice bags, cold saline, esmolol, and dantrolene 60 mg IV; within 10 minutes temperature dropped and rigidity disappeared.",
    "Postoperative course included fever, mild pulmonary edema, leukocytosis, thrombocytopenia, elevated CRP, hypoxemia, sanguineous urine, Klebsiella pneumoniae bacteremia, antibiotics, ICU monitoring, ward transfer on postoperative day 6, and discharge on postoperative day 12."
  ],
